{"arrivo":"et","origine":"urj-fin-pro","origine_nome":"Proto-Finnic","livello2":"ine-bsl-pro","livello2_nome":"Proto-Balto-Slavic","n":12,"parole":[{"parola":"ahas","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"narrow, cramped; of small extent in width","termine_origine":"*ahtas","catena":[{"codice":"urj-fin-pro","nome":"Proto-Finnic","termine":"*ahtas","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"ine-bsl-pro","nome":"Proto-Balto-Slavic","termine":"*anśtas","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*h₂énǵʰus","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Proto-Finnic *ahtas (“narrow, cramped”), borrowed from Proto-Balto-Slavic *anśtas, from Proto-Indo-European *h₂énǵʰus (“narrow, tight”), of both *h₂enǵʰ- (“narrow, tight”) and the suffix *-us. Cognate with Finnish ahdas, Livvi ahtas, Lithuanian ankštas, Polish wąski, and Russian узкий"},{"parola":"hammas","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"tooth (bone formation in the mouth of a person or animal for grabbing and grinding food)","termine_origine":"*hambas","catena":[{"codice":"urj-fin-pro","nome":"Proto-Finnic","termine":"*hambas","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"ine-bsl-pro","nome":"Proto-Balto-Slavic","termine":"*źámbas","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-bsl-pro","ambiti":["scienza"],"via":"","testo":"From Proto-Finnic *hambas, from Proto-Balto-Slavic *źámbas. Doublet of kamm."},{"parola":"harakas","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"magpie (bird of the genus Pica)","termine_origine":"*harakka","catena":[{"codice":"urj-fin-pro","nome":"Proto-Finnic","termine":"*harakka","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"ine-bsl-pro","nome":"Proto-Balto-Slavic","termine":"*śárˀkāˀ","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-bsl-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Proto-Finnic *harakka, derived 